# BOOT-001: exact build backend for reproducible wheel/sdist builds.
#
# This file MUST stay byte-consistent with [build-system].requires in
# pyproject.toml. It is not an alternative source of truth — PEP 517 isolated
# builds read pyproject.toml and ignore this file entirely, so a mismatch here
# would silently produce a wheel built by a different backend than the one whose
# hashes were locked.
#
# Division of labour:
#   pyproject.toml [build-system].requires  -> governs `python -m build`
#                                              (isolated; installs from PyPI)
#   config/requirements-build.lock          -> governs hash-verified builds
#                                              (`--no-isolation` after
#                                               `pip install --require-hashes`)
#
# tools/lock-deps.sh compiles this file, with transitive hashes, into
# config/requirements-build.lock. tools/verify-locks.sh asserts that the exact
# pin here is identical to the exact pin in [build-system].requires.
hatchling==1.31.0
